---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Quick Start" description="Get Engrams running in your project in under five minutes — from zero to schema-guided retrieval.">
  <h1>Quick Start: Cognitive Schemas in 5 Minutes</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    From an empty repository to active cognitive schemas in five simple commands.
    By the end, your AI assistant can plan features, verify contracts, and receive high-level architectural rules before opening source files.
    Make sure you have completed the <a href="/docs/installation">installation</a> first.
  </p>

  <h2>Agent Setup</h2>
  <p>
    Engrams provides a built-in <code>instructions</code> command that outputs the standardized operating protocol for LLM agents:
  </p>
  <pre><code>engrams instructions</code></pre>
  <p>
    Run this in your project root and paste the output directly into your <code>AGENTS.md</code> file, <code>.cursorrules</code>, or system prompt configuration.
  </p>

  <h2>5-Minute Walkthrough</h2>
  <div class="steps">

    <!-- Step 1 -->
    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">1</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Initialize the local database</h3>
        <p>
          Create the embedded SQLite database in your workspace:
        </p>
        <pre><code>engrams init</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 2 -->
    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">2</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Log an architecture decision with an explicit contract</h3>
        <p>
          When introducing an interface, behavior, or adapter, embed its contract so future sessions don't need to read implementation files:
        </p>
        <pre><code>engrams decision log \
  --summary "Provider behavior for payment adapters" \
  --contract "fn process(amount: u64, currency: &amp;str) -> Result&lt;Receipt, PaymentError&gt;" \
  --rationale "Pluggable payment processors across Stripe and PayPal" \
  --tags payment,adapter,api \
  --anchor src/adapters/stripe.rs</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 3 -->
    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">3</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Propose and confirm a Cognitive Schema</h3>
        <p>
          Propose a reviewed schema with a plain-language claim, conditional trigger-and-rule instruction, and scope, then confirm it:
        </p>
        <pre><code>engrams schema propose \
  --members decision:1,decision:2,decision:3 \
  --name payment-adapters \
  --statement "All payment adapters share one idempotent provider contract and strict PII redaction" \
  --trigger "editing payment adapter implementations" \
  --rule "implement PaymentProvider; use Stripe idempotent keys; never log raw card numbers" \
  --scope-paths src/adapters --scope-tags payment,adapter

engrams schema confirm proposal:1</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 4 -->
    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">4</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Intercept edits with schema-guided advice</h3>
        <p>
          Before touching code, your agent runs <code>advise</code>. Engrams surfaces the matching schema above all constraints in under 300 tokens:
        </p>
        <pre><code>engrams advise src/adapters/stripe.rs</code></pre>
        <pre><code>&#123;
  "schemas": [
    &#123;
      "id": 1,
      "name": "payment-adapters",
      "statement": "All payment adapters share one idempotent provider contract and strict PII redaction",
      "summary": "Fires when editing payment adapter implementations: implement PaymentProvider...",
      "scope": &#123; "tags": ["adapter", "payment"], "paths": ["src/adapters"] &#125;,
      "matched_by": &#123; "via": "member_anchor", "value": "src/adapters/stripe.rs" &#125;
    &#125;
  ],
  "constraints": [ ... ],
  "violations": []
&#125;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 5 -->
    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">5</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Close the session, view token ROI, and catch new opportunities</h3>
        <p>
          At session end, record your PR, view your exact schema guidance count, and receive ready-to-fill <code>propose_command</code> templates for new candidate schemas:
        </p>
        <pre><code>engrams session close --pr 42</code></pre>
        <pre><code>&#123;
  "closed": true,
  "schema_value": &#123; "guided_retrievals": 3, "distinct_schemas": 1, "schemas": [&#123; "id": 1, "name": "payment-adapters", "guided": 3 &#125;] &#125;,
  "schema_prompts": [ ... ]
&#125;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

